sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-second-assessor-audit-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Parameter expressivity: 80/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The script demonstrates meaningful parameter control in its analytical stability and amplitude panels: widening the lateral angular spread theta_0 from 0 deg (fig16_odd) to 60 deg (fig17_even) switches the dominant marginal-stability branch from odd to even, and setting lateral_inhibition to 0.0 in evaluate_gaussian_negative_control collapses the interior band-pass wavenumber peak (q* = 1.028, prominence 0.120) to the lower boundary (q_min = 0.050, prominence 0.0). In addition, Panel B continuously sweeps wavevector intersection angle theta across [0, 180] deg to track gamma_3(theta) across the (1/2)*gamma_3(0) roll/lattice stability threshold. However, we deduct 10 points because the four gallery morphologies are selected via discrete hard-coded mode tables (pattern = rings, spiral, cobweb, honeycomb in planform_modes) rather than emerging continuously from sweeping biophysical control parameters with pattern = auto. We deduct 6 points because stability_scan overrides the critical wavenumber q* with a fixed wave_count whenever pattern != auto, decoupling the rendered spatial wavelength in the gallery from the underlying lateral-inhibition kernel parameters. Finally, we deduct 4 points because make_gif claims in its inline comment to perform a continuous angle sweep, but actually holds pattern_angle_deg fixed per preset and only translates the spatial phase over one cycle. Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L635–L645: When pattern != 'auto', wave_number is computed from fixed params.wave_count rather than the critical wavenumber critical_q from the dispersion relation <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L635-L645>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L660–L691: Discrete pattern string switch in planform_modes hard-codes wavevector angles and amplitudes for each form-constant family <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L660-L691>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L880–L898: Gaussian-only negative control (lateral_inhibition=0.0) cleanly demonstrates loss of the interior Turing wavenumber peak <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L880-L898>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L1226–L1233: make_gif comment claims a continuous angle sweep, but the loop only increments spatial phase while keeping pattern_angle_deg fixed <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/68c4a1a/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L1226-L1233>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.8"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-parameter-expressivity> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Parameter expressivity' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dcterms:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

